contentText:
Both Diddy &#8216;s family and the Bureau of Prisons are denying recent reports about the scuffle the incarcerated mogul allegedly got into with fellow inmate Christopher &#8220;Dudus&#8221; Coke, the leader of the infamous Jamaican crime organization the Shower Posse.

Earlier Thursday morning (Oct. 15), The Breakfast Club&#8217;s Loren LoRosa reported that she talked with someone in Diddy&#8217;s family and was told that a fight never happened.

“I spoke to a family member, a family member of Diddy’s, who tells me this story is completely false,” she shared. “There was not a fight at all.” She added that the two inmates are supposedly on separate sides of the New Jersey prison and don&#8217;t usually cross paths. “From what I’m told, there’s not even an investigation on this happening yet,” LoRosa continued. “But they’re on two different sides of Fort Dix. I&#8217;m told that [Coke] is on what they call the east side and Diddy&#8217;s on a whole different side. They wouldn’t even be interacting every single day.”

The Bureau of Prisons seems to confirm this reporting, telling TMZ , &#8220;We can tell you that the story you are referring to is false and did not happen.&#8221;

Diddy&#8217;s team stood by The Breakfast Club &#8216;s reporting and mentioned the statement given by the Bureau of Prisons mentioned above. &#8220;We believe the initial reports were inaccurate, and the family&#8217;s account is consistent with what we&#8217;ve been able to determine,&#8221; they told Billboard . &#8220;The Bureau of Prisons has also publicly stated that the alleged altercation did not occur. We have no information that would contradict those denials.&#8221;

Diddy&#8217;s tentative release date is set for March 8, 2028, and has been seeking a pardon with the help of Mike Tyson, according to the retired boxer.
